Read-only adversarial pre-review of PR #634 in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (branch origin/wp-onboarding-friction; diff with `git diff origin/main...origin/wp-onboarding-friction`). Purpose: find what an automated reviewer would flag next, before the next push. A consolidated local fix is already underway for these two known findings, so do NOT report them: (1) E132 echoing user remote strings, including helper URLs like hg::REDACTED (the fix: never print the raw remote anywhere); (2) the 'run callisto version first' hint must be computed on the exact release roster (selection, group expansion, publishable packages only).

Hunt in the changed code AND the code paths it calls for these recurring classes:
- secrets or user-supplied strings reaching any output (errors, JSON, logs, notes), including Debug impls and miette help/labels;
- dry run, preview or hints computed on a different set or path than the real run (init vs release vs release --dry-run; selection; groups; private/unpublished packages);
- text vs --format json vs non-TTY: JSON stdout must stay one document; human notes once on stderr in both modes;
- validation order and error codes (E132, E214 etc.) matching docs/specs (check docs/specs/*.json criteria the PR touches, e.g. CLI-WF-01, CLI-WF-06);
- optional conveniences failing the command;
- origin handling: missing origin, no remotes, multiple remotes, pushurl vs url, insteadOf rewrites, ssh scp-style with ports, uppercase schemes, trailing .git or slash, GitHub Enterprise hosts;
- Rust: non-exhaustive matches on our enums (_ arms), unwrap/expect, swallowed errors, visibility, needless clones;
- tests that don't actually assert the behaviour.

For each issue: file:line, a concrete scenario (input -> wrong output), and the smallest fix. Verify each against the code before reporting; drop anything speculative. Under 30 lines, most severe first, and say plainly if you find nothing.

